---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
const PREVIEW = Boolean(import.meta.env.MAXWELL_PREVIEW);
---
<Base page="join" title="Join us" description={`How to join ${SITE.name}, how projects run, and how authorship is decided.`}>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">Join us</p>
      <h1>Work with us</h1>
      <p>{SITE.name} is an open group. {SITE.lead.name} leads it and sets the research questions; students and
        researchers carry out the projects, from building the data to writing the paper.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="section" style="border-bottom:0">
    <div class="wrap join-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Who we are looking for</h2>
        <p>Students and researchers who work on large language models or on wireless communications, and who want to
          test what language models can and cannot do on real engineering problems. You do not need both backgrounds,
          and you do not need to be at NTU: the group is open to people at any university or institute.</p>

        <h2>How to start</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Write to {SITE.lead.name}</strong> at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.lead.email}`}>{SITE.lead.email}</a>{" "}
            with a few lines on what you would like to work on and anything you have built before.</li>
          <li><strong>Read one of our papers</strong> closely, ideally the one nearest your interest, and come with a
            question it leaves open.</li>
          <li><strong>Start with a scoped piece</strong> of an existing project before leading your own.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>How projects run</h2>
        <p>There is no fixed meeting schedule. Each project meets when the work needs it, and the people on it agree how
          often.</p>

        <h2>Authorship</h2>
        {PREVIEW && <div class="todo"><b>DRAFT · Xin</b>Wording below is a draft for Xin to confirm.</div>}
        <p>Authorship follows substantive contribution. An author has contributed to the idea, the data, the experiments
          or the analysis, has helped write or revise the paper, and can answer for the work, in the spirit of the
          ICMJE criteria; individual contributions are recorded with the CRediT roles.</p>
        <p>Author order is agreed when a project starts. If contributions change, any change to the order is discussed
          openly and in advance.</p>
        <p>People who contribute to a dataset or benchmark without meeting these criteria are named in its
          acknowledgements or contributor list.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="aside-card" aria-label="Contact">
        <p class="label">Contact</p>
        <p><a href={SITE.lead.url}>{SITE.lead.name}</a><br>{SITE.institution.name}, {SITE.institution.place}</p>
        <p><a href={`mailto:${SITE.lead.email}`}>{SITE.lead.email}</a></p>
        {PREVIEW && <p class="todo" style="margin-top:8px"><b>DRAFT · Xin</b>Contact address to confirm.</p>}
        <p><a href={SITE.github}>GitHub: {SITE.githubName}</a></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
